WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.070
- [Mark] All right, Christine.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.530
Christine, where are you from?

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.050
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.780
- [Christine] I grew up in

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.820
Wichita Falls, Texas.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.990
- [Mark] Wichita Falls, Texas.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.870
And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.803
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:23.863
- Yeah.

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.800
Left when I was quite young.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.870
But...

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.453
- [Mark] How old were you when you left?

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.400
- Like 12, I believe.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.233
- [Mark] 12?

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.066
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:38.066 --> 00:00:39.840
- [Mark] What was going on at home that

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.863
you left at 12?

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.810
- I was forced to leave home

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.910
because I had a young child,

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.890
and there was a lot of
fighting and arguing at home.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:53.180
- [Mark] You got pregnant at 12?

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.760
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.930
- [Mark] Who is the father?

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:57.770
- His name is...

00:01:02.808 --> 00:01:05.120
- [Mark] So you had a baby?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.300
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.553
- [Mark] And where'd you go
at 12 years old with the baby?

00:01:10.346 --> 00:01:11.230
- I

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.063
moved to

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.853
Denver for a while.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.560
- [Mark] Your family wouldn't help you?

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.393
- No.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:24.890
- [Mark] What was your childhood like?

00:01:26.658 --> 00:01:28.963
- It was was a bit rough at times.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.290
There was a lot of arguing
and strife at home,

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.730
- [Mark] Any abuse, like sexual
abuse or anything like that?

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.563
- Yeah. Some, yeah.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.910
- [Mark] With who? With your relatives?

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.153
- Yeah.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.510
- [Mark] So you moved to Denver
as a mother at 12 years old?

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.360
You two?
- Yeah.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.633
- [Mark] And what'd you do then?

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.040
- I did my best to

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.900
raise my oldest daughter

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.733
and

00:02:14.268 --> 00:02:15.851
I struggled some...

00:02:22.065 --> 00:02:22.898
Yeah.

00:02:27.977 --> 00:02:30.727
I don't know, it was rough but...

00:02:33.397 --> 00:02:34.333
- [Mark] Where'd you keep the baby?

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:37.460
- I ended up giving the
baby up for adoption

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.563
'cause she was getting
raped by her grandpa.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.030
- [Mark] This is the father's father?

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:51.863
- Yeah.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.143
- [Mark] And then where'd
you go from there?

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.110
- I left for a while to Texas,

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.723
like back to Texas for a bit.

00:03:05.578 --> 00:03:08.068
But,

00:03:08.068 --> 00:03:08.901
yeah.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.690
- [Mark] How far did you go in school?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.733
- Sixth grade.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.059
- [Mark] And drugs are a
part of your life today?

00:03:21.059 --> 00:03:23.029
- Yeah,

00:03:23.029 --> 00:03:23.862
they are.

00:03:26.078 --> 00:03:28.390
- [Mark] And that's crystal meth?

00:03:29.784 --> 00:03:30.617
- Yeah.

00:03:30.617 --> 00:03:31.450
- [Mark] When did that start for you?

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.103
Or when did drug use start for you?

00:03:33.103 --> 00:03:34.853
- When I was like 11.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.353
- [Mark] Who introduced
you to drugs at 11?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.573
- My parents.

00:03:45.717 --> 00:03:47.095
- [Mark] So your parents were addicts?

00:03:47.095 --> 00:03:47.928
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.441
- [Mark] So today you're
living on Skid Row?

00:03:52.441 --> 00:03:53.274
- I am.

00:03:53.274 --> 00:03:55.093
- [Mark] You're in a tent or
you're just on the street?

00:03:55.093 --> 00:03:58.923
- Just really on the street right now.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.623
Nowhere really to go.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.183
- [Mark] And what are you
doing to support yourself?

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.403
- Typically,

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.793
- [Mark] What a lot of the girls do?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.137
- I guess, in a way.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:38.970
- [Mark] Do you have any
contact with your family at all?

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.298
- I do not, not right now.

00:04:41.298 --> 00:04:42.131
- [Mark] You don't?

00:04:42.131 --> 00:04:42.964
When is the last time you spoke to anyone?

00:04:42.964 --> 00:04:44.763
- It's been quite some time.

00:04:46.964 --> 00:04:48.584
- [Mark] And you have other children too?

00:04:48.584 --> 00:04:49.480
- I do.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.750
- [Mark] How many kids do you have?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.523
- Other than Rissa,

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:55.823
I have five.

00:04:56.805 --> 00:04:57.638
- [Mark] You have five.

00:04:57.638 --> 00:04:58.493
And did you raise the other ones?

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.910
- One was my (mumbles) father

00:05:06.134 --> 00:05:09.410
and I raised the last part of it, yeah.

00:05:13.454 --> 00:05:14.380
- [Mark] How old are you today?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.213
- 41.

00:05:15.213 --> 00:05:16.521
- [Mark] 41.

00:05:16.521 --> 00:05:18.673
And your kids range in
age from what to what?

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.643
- The oldest 30.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:23.570
And

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.833
30,

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.673
maybe 30 And the youngest 13, I believe.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.520
- [Mark] Do you talk
with any of your kids?

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.120
- [Christine] No, not right now.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.437
- [Mark] Living here on the
street is a terrible life.

00:05:41.437 --> 00:05:42.270
- [Christine] It is.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.810
- [Mark] What kind of stuff
have you been through?

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.151
- [Christine] I've been through

00:05:45.151 --> 00:05:46.551
pretty much everything like,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:49.833
rape.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:56.053
Just a bunch of trauma, I guess.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.973
- [Mark] What's the hardest
part of your life right now?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.563
- [Christine] Not permanently like having,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.500
like the inability to be able
to like take showers and like,

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.573
it's rough.

00:06:23.811 --> 00:06:24.693
- [Mark] Do you have any friends?

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.210
- [Christine] A few.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.043
Like,

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:33.663
they are...

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:36.840
- [Mark] Just people on the street?

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:37.790
- [Christine] Yeah.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.520
- [Mark] Do you feel like you
were ever loved in your life?

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.160
- [Christine] Yeah.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:50.993
Like by

00:06:59.030 --> 00:06:59.923
friends.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.130
- [Mark] Do you have anyone in your life

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.530
that you feel you can trust?

00:07:14.214 --> 00:07:15.740
Friends on the street are not
always the most trustworthy.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.310
- The best, right?

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.703
And I (mumbles) it's rough,

00:07:19.936 --> 00:07:20.769
but yeah.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.870
- [Mark] What's the most
important lesson you've learned

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:29.103
in your 41 years?

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:32.813
- That

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:40.740
to never like give up hope on anything,

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.833
especially even when terrible
things happen it seams.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.230
- [Mark] You get depressed sometimes?

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.063
- I do.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.874
- [Mark] It must be tough.

00:07:52.874 --> 00:07:53.707
- Yeah.

00:07:56.222 --> 00:07:57.055
- [Mark] Do you feel sometimes

00:07:57.055 --> 00:07:59.772
you're just repeating the
same life your parents had?

00:07:59.772 --> 00:08:00.605
- Yeah.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.250
- [Mark] It feels like a
generational curse, right?

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.950
- It does, in a way.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.550
- [Mark] How do you see this,

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.483
bad role models that you had as a kid?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.673
- Yeah.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.840
- [Mark] Looking back at your childhood,

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.657
is there anything you
wish had been different?

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.653
- That

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.443
I would have done better
with the kids, I believe.

00:08:30.756 --> 00:08:32.420
Like you never feel like...

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.780
Sometimes you want to
be the perfect parent

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:37.320
and it's almost impossible, but yeah,

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.570
I think that would be
the one thing I regret.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.600
- [Mark] Do you ever feel
like life is just unfair?

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.750
- Yeah.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.583
Absolutely.

00:08:50.987 --> 00:08:51.820
Like

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.033
not being able to,

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.030
have freedom like to
just be happy and like

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.673
in love with whom you wish and

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.113
free of

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.710
like crazy burdens.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.910
You know what I mean?

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:16.053
- [Mark] Do you feel betrayed
by members of your family?

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.433
- In a way.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.750
I've been hurt by them,

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:24.583
but

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.010
not like...

00:09:31.497 --> 00:09:32.330
- [Mark] Are you still hopeful?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.163
- I am.

00:09:33.163 --> 00:09:34.240
- [Mark] You are. That's good.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.200
What do you hope for?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.310
- I hope to...

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.030
like be able to

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.230
dance and sing and like

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.470
do other stuff, it'd be nice.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:52.470
But yeah, that's what I really hope for.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.120
You know what I mean?

00:09:55.061 --> 00:09:56.130
- [Mark] What was the
best time of your life?

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.280
- The best time of my
life would have been,

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.253
probably

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.550
when I was

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:32.720
16,

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:33.810
and it was probably

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.253
being an assistant kindergarten teacher.

00:10:44.079 --> 00:10:45.070
That was probably the best time of my life

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.543
is helping out the kids.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:50.798
But yeah.

00:10:50.798 --> 00:10:51.631
- [Mark] Have you had jobs?

00:10:51.631 --> 00:10:53.523
- Yeah, I've been an accounting clerk.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:11:01.150
I've

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:07.510
worked at gas stations, little
things like that, but...

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:15.280
- [Mark] Is this the worst
time of your life right now?

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:16.190
- Yeah.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.600
- [Mark] It's pretty rough.

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:18.433
- Yeah.

00:11:18.433 --> 00:11:20.850
Absolutely like hard and just...

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.270
- [Mark] Do you feel like you're worthy

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.610
of a better life than this?

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:29.353
- I hope so, yeah.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.120
- [Mark] I think everyone is.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.409
- Right?

00:11:33.409 --> 00:11:34.242
- [Mark] But sometimes people,

00:11:34.242 --> 00:11:35.933
some people feel like they
just don't deserve it,

00:11:37.889 --> 00:11:39.628
and they belong here on the street.

00:11:39.628 --> 00:11:42.100
- Yeah.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.780
- [Mark] You've been
homeless for how long?

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:44.930
- For about a year now.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.523
- [Mark] Does it feel like home?

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:54.873
- Not really.

00:12:09.324 --> 00:12:14.241
I hope for a better future than
just living on the streets.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.340
- [Mark] What's the most dangerous
thing you've encountered?

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.260
- Being raped

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.200
by some friends,

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.750
I guess.

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:30.583
Yeah.

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.960
- [Mark] How do you see
yourself changing your life

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.310
and getting away from here?

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:46.423
- Getting cleaned up and like,

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.660
turn the best that I can.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:58.900
Need to at least get a
little started somehow,

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:00.873
have money later,

00:13:02.485 --> 00:13:03.400
get an apartment.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.490
I have no idea.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.323
Something,

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.033
I have no idea.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.610
- [Mark] What personality
trait do you have

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:13.780
that helps you survive

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.270
this street life?

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.860
- [Christine] Just having a
positive attitude, I guess.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:24.810
- [Mark] You stay positive?

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:25.643
- [Christine] Yeah.

00:13:25.643 --> 00:13:26.623
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:30.443
All right, Christine.

00:13:30.443 --> 00:13:31.600
And thank you for talking with me.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:32.540
- You're welcome.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:36.400
- [Mark] Good luck with
getting out of here.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:37.233
- Thank you.

00:13:37.233 --> 00:13:38.066
- [Mark] Thank you very much.

00:13:38.066 --> 00:13:39.314
- You're welcome.

